    "body": "> How is it different from `import.meta.resolve('image.jpg')`\r\n\r\nGood question. The semantics would actually be the same. One piece of motivation is that this form is more \"declarative\"-looking and therefore statically analyzable (which should mostly help build tools, given that not enough information is available for a prefetcher to use this). See more information about motivation (for a previous iteration of this idea) at https://github.com/tc39/proposal-asset-references . Also note that some people in TC39 are considering whether we should propose some other syntax for this, besides using import attributes.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
