    "created_at": "2024-11-12T23:19:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-12T23:19:26Z",
    "body": "I find it reasonable to enable or even encourage `import` `with` `type` `bytes` to also specify the expected MIME type, possibly with another attribute like `mimeType` so that the module cannot be deceived into misinterpreting the imported content, especially for dynamic import, for example, `import(location, { with: { type: 'bytes', mimeType: 'image/png' } })`. I would want the `mimeType` assertion to be optional since not all binary data that modules can usefully interpret has a MIME type, except insofar as `application/octet-stream` is sufficiently abstract to apply to anything.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
